A</given-names></name><name><surname>Panaretakis</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tufi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Joza</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>van Endert</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghiringhelli</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Apetoh</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Chaput</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Flament</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ullrich</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>de Botton</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zitvogel</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kroemer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ecto-calreticulin in immunogenic chemotherapy</article-title><source>Immunol Rev</source><year>2007</year><volume>220</volume><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17979837</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1600-065X.2007.00567.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ghali</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>WB</given-names></name><name><surname>Torre-Amione</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Haynos</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Rayburn</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Amato</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cowart</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Valentini</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Carminati</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gheorghiade</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A phase 1&#x02013;2 dose-escalating study evaluating the safety and tolerability of istaroxime and specific effects on electrocardiographic and hemodynamic parameters in patients with chronic heart failure with reduced systolic function</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>47A</fpage><lpage>56A</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17239705</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.amjcard.2006.09.006</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>